From: Panurus maintainers
Subject: [PATCH 9/10] lnp_quad_verify, abdlop_verify: bound z21

The verifiers bounded only z22 = w - gamma * w1, never z21, the A2' part of
the opening sent in the proof, while the prover rejects on and the
parameters assume a bound on all of z2 = (z21, z22)
(lazer-crypto/lazer#26). They now check
l2(z21)^2 + l2(w - gamma * w1)^2 <= Bsqr. Honest proofs satisfy it; the
transcript does not change.

Panurus-local patch, applied by `make lazer-install` (lazer.mk).

diff --git a/src/abdlop.c b/src/abdlop.c
index ffde7af..66501aa 100644
--- a/src/abdlop.c
+++ b/src/abdlop.c
@@ -456,6 +456,7 @@ abdlop_verify (uint8_t hash[32], poly_t c, polyvec_t z1, polyvec_t z21,
   polyvec_t w1, tmp1;
   poly_t tmp2, c2;
   INT_T (l2sqr, nlimbs * 2);
+  INT_T (l2sqrz21, nlimbs * 2);
   INT_T (bnd, nlimbs * 2);
   INT_T (linf, nlimbs);
   INT_T (tmp, 1);
@@ -534,8 +535,15 @@ abdlop_verify (uint8_t hash[32], poly_t c, polyvec_t z1, polyvec_t z21,
   if (!b)
     goto ret;
 
+  /*
+   * the prover rejects on l2(z21,z22)^2 <= Bsqr and the parameters bound all
+   * of z2: z21 must be bounded too, not only z22 = w - gamma*w1 (panurus
+   * patch, lazer-crypto/lazer#26). Honest proofs are unaffected.
+   */
   polyvec_subscale (tmp1, gamma, w1, 0);
   polyvec_l2sqr (l2sqr, tmp1);
+  polyvec_l2sqr (l2sqrz21, z21);
+  int_add (l2sqr, l2sqr, l2sqrz21);
   b = int_le (l2sqr, params->Bsqr);
   if (!b)
     goto ret;
